{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01048",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 4.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Good morning. I've just opened your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.1,
      "end_seconds": 7.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.94,
      "end_seconds": 10.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Lovely day outside, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.46,
      "end_seconds": 21.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Yeah, it is, I almost forgot I was coming here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.67,
      "end_seconds": 26.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.46,
      "end_seconds": 38.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.54,
      "text": "So, um, mainly skipped beats. There's a couple of other things, but that's the the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.05,
      "end_seconds": 41.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.92,
      "end_seconds": 52.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.14,
      "text": "It's, It's Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid. I take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.5,
      "end_seconds": 53.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "mm-hmm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.87,
      "end_seconds": 58.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I take herbal calming tea, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.2,
      "end_seconds": 62.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.75,
      "end_seconds": 66.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "well, I've had it for five days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.98,
      "end_seconds": 76.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.89,
      "end_seconds": 95.43,
      "duration_seconds": 14.54,
      "text": "right, about a five out of ten. It's every other day. Caffeine definitely sets it off. There was being a bit anxious, yes, but that went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.16,
      "end_seconds": 99.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "have you had any fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.97,
      "end_seconds": 103.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.92,
      "end_seconds": 109.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "And what about chest pain, shortness of breath or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.96,
      "end_seconds": 112.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.35,
      "end_seconds": 114.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.93,
      "end_seconds": 121.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.52,
      "end_seconds": 124.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.96,
      "end_seconds": 135.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "So, I have an underactive thyroid, for nearly five years. Yes, arthritis in my knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.03,
      "end_seconds": 143.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.44,
      "end_seconds": 146.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.08,
      "end_seconds": 158.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.98,
      "end_seconds": 163.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.58,
      "end_seconds": 170.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.23,
      "end_seconds": 183.98,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I work in accounts at a hospital. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I swim twice a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.9,
      "end_seconds": 188.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "So, I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.9,
      "end_seconds": 201.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.2,
      "end_seconds": 225.17,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "okay: height 155 centimetres, pressure 121 over 77, BMI works out to 34.1. And pulse 71, temperature 36.7, weight 82 kilos"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.98,
      "end_seconds": 227.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.32,
      "end_seconds": 232.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.37,
      "end_seconds": 236.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.23,
      "end_seconds": 240.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.55,
      "end_seconds": 253.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.95,
      "end_seconds": 255.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.65,
      "end_seconds": 261.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.92,
      "end_seconds": 284.61,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I don't have a clear answer today: harmless extra heartbeats is possible, and so is an anxiety-related palpitation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.82,
      "end_seconds": 313.7,
      "duration_seconds": 21.88,
      "text": "I want an ECG done, that's for palpitations cut back on coffee and energy drinks and keep a diary of when it happens please don't wait if you faint or have chest pain that's when to be seen urgently anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.4,
      "end_seconds": 319.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}